{"id": "EUVD-2026-103323", "enisaUuid": "552f4700-d8ca-38b0-aa85-c868e92467a4", "description": "phpMyFAQ from 4.2.0-alpha before 4.2.0-beta contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability in SvgSanitizer that allows FAQ editors to store executable SVG files. Attackers can split script tags around removed tokens like processing instructions so single-pass removal reassembles them, executing script in the application origin when victims open the file.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:40:09", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-95fm-rwq4-rxrf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-4.2.0-alpha-before-4.2.0-beta-stored-xss-via-svg-upload-sanitizer-bypass"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111896", "GHSA-fch3-7f9r-g5gg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "53821502-7ddf-36e3-817b-ddb52eb11bba", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "afd8b11e-7942-346f-8426-3787c364e9f9", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}